WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:02.040
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:09.370
Welcome to what was the most densely populated
place on Earth, Kowloon Walled City was home

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:15.379
to over 33,000 people, all crammed into a
measly six-acres.

00:00:15.379 --> 00:00:18.280
It sat right in the middle of Hong Kong.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:23.369
Manila, the capital city of the Philippines
currently holds the title of the world’s

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:28.930
most densely populated place, but that’s
only because Kowloon Walled City was demolished

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:30.769
in 1994.

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:33.900
Prior to this it held the title for over 20
years.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.910
But this mish-mash of buildings, cobbled together
from scrap materials was one of the most interesting

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.530
communities on the planet.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:43.720
It was no ordinary slum.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.900
It’s thousands of residents lived toe-to-toe
with crime and the weird and wonderful.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.230
It was a self-sustained city, like a world
within a world.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:58.170
Let’s take a trip down the alleyways of
this incredible shanty town and uncover its

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.170
secrets.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:03.020
But first, how the hell did THIS happen?

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:08.660
Kowloon Walled City has a long and intricate
history and like any good tale from history,

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:11.120
it all started with the British.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:16.390
Hong Kong island was ceded to the British
in 1841 as part of the Treaty of Nanjing,

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.640
that ended the Opium War.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:24.640
However, China wouldn’t give the British
Kowloon Walled City and held onto it for military

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.482
use and they built a wall around it, hence
the “Walled” bit.

00:01:28.482 --> 00:01:33.680
Kowloon Walled City began life as a salt trading
outpost during the Song Dynasty, all the way

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:34.680
back in 960.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:41.650
And it remained a small, forgotten outpost
for hundreds of years, until the British got

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.710
their invasive hands on Hong Kong.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:49.460
As you can imagine, being a tiny Chinese owned
settlement, entirely surrounded by a foreign

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.140
country caused some issues.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:56.270
The British found the Walled City a curiosity.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:01.560
They affectionately called it “Chinese Town”
– seriously, they named it this on maps

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.020
of Hong Kong.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:07.380
It became somewhat of a tourist attraction
for British Colonials.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:12.650
So how did it turn into this… and what happened
to the wall?

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:18.519
Well during World War II, amidst the Japanese
occupation of Hong Kong, the Japanese demolished

00:02:18.519 --> 00:02:20.469
the stone walls of the settlement.

00:02:20.469 --> 00:02:27.520
As to its extremely dense population, well
that happened because of a political peculiarity

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:34.689
– because Kowloon was a Chinese nation surrounded
by a British overseas territory it was impossible

00:02:34.689 --> 00:02:36.240
for China to police the area.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:41.159
And because it didn’t belong to the British,
they couldn’t care less what went on within

00:02:41.159 --> 00:02:42.279
its perimeter.

00:02:42.279 --> 00:02:47.519
This made Kowloon Walled City essentially
lawless.

00:02:47.519 --> 00:02:52.780
Thousands of refugees from the Chinese Civic
War of the 1940s came to live in Kowloon Walled

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:58.560
City – it was perfect, since it was essentially
Chinese, but it’s residents were surrounded

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.129
and protected by the British.

00:03:01.129 --> 00:03:06.849
Since there were no rules or laws, people
self-built rooms to live in, wherever they

00:03:06.849 --> 00:03:08.209
could find a space.

00:03:08.209 --> 00:03:13.329
There was absolutely no order – if there
was a space free, then somebody was bound

00:03:13.329 --> 00:03:18.670
to build their own Kowloon penthouse there,
no matter how cramped it would be.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:22.980
And when all the floor space was filled, they
simply built upwards.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:26.659
All the way up to 14 stories high.

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:30.999
They would have kept going if not for the
nearby airport that said they needed the airspace

00:03:30.999 --> 00:03:35.709
above Kowloon to be kept empty due to airplane
traffic.

00:03:35.709 --> 00:03:40.370
The whole structure is quite an impressive
piece of engineering, considering it was built

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:41.999
by ordinary citizens.

00:03:41.999 --> 00:03:46.919
They even assembled a gigantic maze of water
pipes to bring running water into everyone’s

00:03:46.919 --> 00:03:47.919
homes.

00:03:47.919 --> 00:03:53.999
In a world with no police to keep watch, crime
and business flourished, often as the same

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:55.019
entity.

00:03:55.019 --> 00:04:00.629
Within no time at all the city became ruled
by organized crime syndicates, the Triads.

00:04:00.629 --> 00:04:06.069
The slum became littered with endless brothels,
gambling parlours and opium dens.

00:04:06.069 --> 00:04:11.080
Even more disturbing is that due to a lack
of space, during the day these same rooms

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:17.400
were used as schools and hair salons; during
the night, they were strip clubs and brothels.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:22.479
But it wasn’t just outlets of criminality
that lined this endless warren of hidden alleyways

00:04:22.479 --> 00:04:23.780
and courtyards.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.900
Genuine businesses thrived here too.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:32.020
It became a self-sustained, tightly knit community
with hundreds of shops selling anything you

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.449
could imagine.

00:04:33.449 --> 00:04:39.590
Hundreds of products were manufactured within
the walls, dog-meat, fish balls, noodle makers,

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:45.710
you name it, all free to produce and sell
to the rest of Hong Kong without any fire,

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:48.250
health or labour safety laws.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:54.980
But above all else, it was known for two things,
unlicensed dentists and doctors.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:05:00.470
Due to the virtually non-existent laws within
Kowloon, you didn’t need a license to setup

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:06.000
shop as a “professional” dentist or doctor,
which made for some rather dubious places

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.460
to get your fillings done.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:12.490
Hong Kong residents who couldn’t afford
the high healthcare costs in the actual city,

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:15.700
went to Kowloon Walled City to get it done
on the cheap.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:20.729
Which is probably not a very smart idea, considering
absolutely zero qualifications were needed

00:05:20.729 --> 00:05:22.310
to practice here.

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:27.180
Conditions within the slum weren’t comfortable
at the best of times, because the accommodation

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:33.870
had been built so high, and so unevenly, there
was absolutely zero natural light at the bottom

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:38.030
levels, and most residents lived without sunlight
24/7.

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:42.740
Children would play on the roof, which was
incredibly dangerous, with gaps between buildings

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:47.960
that had been shoved together, and endless
dangerous items protruding from the ground.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:54.759
Eventually the filthy, cramped urban maze
that thousands called home was demolished.

00:05:54.759 --> 00:06:04.639
In 1993 both Britain and China mutually agreed
to demolish Kowloon Walled City.

00:06:04.639 --> 00:06:07.830
Residents were given a small amount of monetary
compensation.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:13.610
In its place now, a public garden called Kowloon
Walled City Park – there’s even a small

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:28.060
memorial of the goliath structure that was
once the most inhabited six-acres on Earth.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:41.340
Thanks for watching.

